  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Ink Manga Page",
    "overview": "\n**Creative North Star: \"The Ink Manga Page\"**\n\nEvery core page reads as a page of black-and-white seinen line art. Content sits in heavy ink panel frames on white paper; what is \"now\" (the urgent exam, today's calendar cell, the current class, the wide panel) is toned with diagonal pen hatching; secondary tone is grey hatching and halftone dots. The next action on each page is spoken from a speech bubble with a solid ink tail, and every other panel follows it.\n\nOne colour is allowed on the page, and it is not chosen by the designer: it is sampled from the owner's Today cover image, so the whole site re-inks itself when the cover changes. With no cover, the default is an ink red. The dark theme is the same page inverted: near-black paper, off-white ink. Course tones (five pale categorical colours) mark which subject a tag, class block or subject cover belongs to, always with black text on them.\n\nDensity is a study tool, not a dashboard: one wide panel per row of narrower ones (manga page rhythm, not an equal tile grid), large Kaisei Decol numerals first, short UI labels in Zen Maru Gothic. The old Notion-pastel look (emoji tiles, pastel gradients, sparkle headings, equal grids) is the confirmed anti-reference.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "3px ink panel frames with near-square 2px corners; no soft shadows on panels.",
      "Pen hatching in the cover accent marks \"now\"; grey hatching and halftone dots are secondary tone.",
      "A speech-bubble lead panel opens every core page with the next step.",
      "One accent colour, derived from the owner's cover, with contrast computed at runtime.",
      "Kaisei Decol for display and numerals; Zen Maru Gothic (Mali for Thai) for UI.",
      "Dark theme is an inverted page, not a separate palette."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Borrowed Ink Rule",
        "body": "The accent is never hard-coded. Every accent shade is built from `--ah`/`--as`/`--al`/`--ad`; a new surface reads `var(--acc)`, `var(--acc-ink)`, `var(--acc-soft)`, `var(--acc-t)` and nothing else, so it re-inks with the cover.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Colour Rule",
        "body": "Black is the primary colour (primary buttons, active nav). The accent is reserved for urgency, \"now\" hatching and the single lead action on a page.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Black-On-Tone Rule",
        "body": "Text on a course tone is always `#111`, in dark mode too.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Numbers In Kaisei Rule",
        "body": "Every count, countdown, score, grade and clock is set in Kaisei Decol; UI words never are.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Eyebrow Rule",
        "body": "Uppercase small caps label table columns and weekdays only; they never sit above a heading as a kicker.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Drawn Depth Rule",
        "body": "\"Now\" is shown by hatching, never by a shadow or glow. Text placed on hatching sits on a paper knockout (`.ko`, or `background: var(--panel)` with 0 4px padding).",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** frame every panel in 3px ink with 2px corners on paper.",
      "**Do** build accent colours only from `--ah`/`--as`/`--al`/`--ad` (via `--acc`, `--acc-ink`, `--acc-soft`, `--acc-t`) so the page follows the cover.",
      "**Do** open each core page with the speech-bubble lead panel and one Go action.",
      "**Do** mark \"now\" with accent hatching and put text on hatching over a paper knockout.",
      "**Do** set counts, countdowns, scores and the clock in Kaisei Decol; UI words in Zen Maru Gothic.",
      "**Do** keep black for primary buttons and the active nav pill; reserve the accent for urgency and the lead action.",
      "**Do** print `#111` on course tones in both themes."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use soft drop shadows or glows on panels; depth is drawn.",
      "**Don't** hard-code an accent hex or hue in page CSS.",
      "**Don't** return to the Notion-pastel look: emoji icons or emoji tiles, pastel gradients, sparkle headings, equal tile grids.",
      "**Don't** put an uppercase eyebrow or kicker above a heading.",
      "**Don't** set the accent as small body text on paper; use `--acc-t` (large or bold text only).",
      "**Don't** round panels beyond 2px or controls beyond 6px."
    ]
  }
}